Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Added. On a device without Steam (not installed, or never started), X Play starts the game in shadPS4 itself, full
screen, with the command its Steam shortcut has (shortcuts.command(), core's platform.start_program() outside the
app's bundle; owner, 30-10-2026: a fallback, as a game cannot be played without Steam otherwise). Without shadPS4
installed it says to install it first. With Steam installed X plays through Steam as before.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 12:54:34

Fixed. Steam started by the app signs in (core, owner, 30-10-2026): X Play and the restart after Steam's shortcuts
changed started steam.exe by the lower-case name in Steam's registry key, and a Steam started so never signed in, its
login window off the screen; it is started by its name as on the disk now, outside the app's bundle. The information
popup's text box is as high as its text, up to 0.7 of the window: a text with "[PS4] <title>" in it was measured as
HTML and kept four lines high.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 01:30:27

Release 1.1.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 00:58:35

Added. The system modules are put in Games\PS4\Modules (owner, 30-10-2026: fixed folders for what the emulator
needs, no folder selecting): the app makes the folder and copies the new or changed .sprx files into shadPS4's module
folder by itself when it opens and each time the shadPS4 card gets the focus (userdata.sync_modules(),
library.modules_home()); the status line says how many it took, and names the folder while modules are missing.

Breaking. No folder is chosen or browsed to any more (owner, 30-10-2026): LB Modules and its browser, and LB Folders
with its added folders, usual places and folder browser, are gone; Your games looks only in Games\PS4 (the user's and
each SD card's), and folders added before are no longer looked in. LB on Your games is Steam artwork now. The Log
pane shows where Games\PS4 is (library.folders(), set_folders(), suggested() and game_folders() removed).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 00:42:29

Added. The app's own game folder (owner, 30-10-2026: drop the games and packages there, no browsing): Games\PS4 in
the user's folder, made when the app opens, and Games\PS4 on each SD card or USB drive that has one, always looked in
and first on LB Folders (library.fixed(), game_folders()); folders can still be added. A package there that waits is a
short row of Your games, "PKG" (a game that needs to be unpacked to play) or "PKG update" (an update its game
lacks: that version is not beside it); X Unpack all unpacks every one, the games first, then each update beside its
game wherever it is, in a folder named like the game's with -UPDATE (an older update there replaced), A Unpack one
(extract.waiting(), place(); unpack(beside=)). A package unpacked without a missing file is deleted (owner,
30-10-2026). Add-ons are left out. The information of Your games says what PKG means.

Breaking. RB Packages, the packages browser on the shadPS4 pane with its places and its page for several packages,
is gone: the packages are put in Games\PS4 and unpacked from Your games (extract.read_all(), plan(), Step and
library.targets() removed).

Fixed. Play and Open Steam start a Steam that does not run plainly, then hand it the game once it has signed in
(core's steam.open_url(); owner, 30-10-2026: after a reboot Steam showed "Updating Steam" and stopped). A package's
row is short enough not to be cut off (owner, 30-10-2026), and the information popup is larger (core).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 00:10:48

Added. RB Remove game on a game of Your games (owner, 30-10-2026: Lumines Remastered no longer plays on shadPS4
0.20.0, and there was no way to take it off the list): the first press asks for five seconds and names the folders
that go; the second takes the game out of Steam and deletes its folder with its update, patch and mods beside it, off
the window's thread (library.removal(), library.delete(), read-only files too). The saves, the play time and the
package stay. A game whose folder is a game folder of the list, a drive, or holds another game is never deleted: the
status line says to delete it by hand. A game package in the game folders whose game is not unpacked yet is a row of
Your games, "not unpacked" (owner, 30-10-2026: Galaga's folder held only its .pkg and showed 0 games), and A Unpack
unpacks it into the folder it is in, the files counted on the pane's line (extract.waiting(); an update waiting
beside its game's package is not listed, so it never takes the game's folder).

Breaking. RB Steam artwork is on the folders now (LB Folders, then RB), since RB on a game removes it.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 23:14:12

